            "review_title": "Review at Couchsurfing Cafe",
            "review_text": "JSTrip_77\nSarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina1194 contributions\n1\nHip Cafe - Quiet Place to Relax with Friends\nMay 2019 • Solo\nHanoi has coffee shops everywhere you look. It's actually hard NOT to find one. However, Couch Surfing Cafe is a step above - literally. Since it's not at street level but on the second and third floors of a building off of Ngoc Khan, you get the cafe experience without the street noise. I actually sat on a second floor balcony because the air quality was good that day. The service was fast and friendly. The wait staff apologized that they didn't have a menu in English but they spoke English so it wasn't a big deal. Plus, I knew what I was going to get anyway. I didn't actually check out the third floor because I was in a bit of a rush to get back to class but the second floor was very charming with several different rooms with different decor - and a very large, clean bathroom. Now that I know how close this place is to my school, I'll be back very soon.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 13, 2019",
